  "provenance": "Exact clean A/B commit+tree and equal native/Cargo/lock/build-tool inputs. Build JS separately. Build one common native addon from A per host, hash it, copy exact bytes to B and stage through existing stage-host-native script. Root+matching native tarballs from package:smoke for each arm installed offline in separate neutral consumers using isolatedConsumerEnv and --ignore-scripts --omit=optional. Both versions0.21.1, source pins, full dist/addon hashes, tarballSHA512 and lockintegrities verified before/after every child, plus final source/dist/native recheck. Record Node24.21.0,pnpm12.4.2,Rust/LLVM hashes,OS/kernel/CPU/availableParallelism/FS/Windowsvolume. Shared native bytes reduce irrelevant nativebuild variance; the changed TSdist must never be shared.",
  "qualification": "Run focused safety-inventory on eachhost+arm with requirednative (candidateowner regression onlyB; commonbaseline suite exactsame). Both package:smoke runs plus installed qualify.mjs rows. Windows actual8 native denial rows required; simulated platform tests complementary. Existing/no-parent mkdirfalse/deniedprefix/refusal and atomiccollision retain sentinels and no temp names. Product builds/tests happen only remotely under parent authorization.",
  "processes": "Linux uses unchanged reviewed step-owner/bounded/settlement controls. Windows uses narrow suspended-start JobObject owner with direct file handles; separately managed-review before dispatch. All steps must join root and descendantjob/group before nextleg/artifacts; any missing settlement blocks success. Build/tool steps may use standard bounded GHAsteps; timed child is freshNode perleg.",
  "publication": "Archive only settled private evidence; retain all failed/incomplete receipts. On failure stop first, no laterlegs. Parent carrier must validate control receipts and finalized archive before upload, exclude workspace fixtures/node_modules/cargo targets.",
  "idle": "Before timing only, parent ensures no concurrent build/test/workloads; record host telemetry. No automated rerun or adaptive perleg wait."
